Discord Messenger for IRIX
==========================

Discord Messenger (https://github.com/DiscordMessenger/dm), the Discord-
compatible messenger for old versions of Windows, ported to IRIX 6.5 with a
Motif user interface.

Run:     /usr/local/bin/discord-messenger
Needs:   IRIX 6.5.22 or later, X11 and IRIX's Motif (x_eoe, motif_eoe);
         any MIPS CPU.  Nothing else: every library it uses besides IRIX's
         is linked into the program.

Logging in: the first start asks you to scan a QR code with the Discord
app on your phone (tap your avatar, then Scan QR Code).  Discord sometimes
asks for a captcha at the end of that, which this program cannot show;
then use "Use a Token Instead": the token is the "authorization" header of
any request a logged-in discord.com page makes (the browser's developer
tools, Network).  It is kept in ~/.discordmessenger/settings.json, readable
only by you.

Note: third-party clients are against Discord's terms of service.  The
risk of a ban is low, but it is there, and it is yours.

What it shows: servers (with their icons), channels, the member list and
messages, with Discord's formatting, replies, reactions, embeds, image
attachments, avatars and colour emoji (Noto Color Emoji).  Colours follow
your desktop's Motif scheme.  View > Larger/Smaller Text sets the text
size; View > Server List, Channel List and Member List show or hide those.
A click on a picture opens it in a window of its own (it scales with the
window); a click on a reaction adds or takes back yours; right-clicking a
message offers Add Reaction (common emoji and the server's own) and Reply.
The client opens the server and channel you were last in.

Files:   ~/.discordmessenger: settings.json, motif.conf (text size and
         the lists View shows) and cache/: pictures (64 MB at most,
         DM_CACHE_MB changes that) and messages/, the newest 200 messages
         of each channel opened (32 MB at most, DM_HISTORY_MB; DM_NO_HISTORY=1
         keeps none).  A channel shows its saved messages at once while its
         newest are fetched.  File > Log Out empties both.
         /usr/local/lib/discord-messenger: fonts/ (DejaVu, Noto Color
         Emoji; DM_FONT_DIR names another directory), cacert.pem (the
         roots of trust; DM_CA_FILE names another file), licenses/.
Links:   open in the browser that DM_BROWSER or BROWSER names.
Debugging: DM_DEBUG=1 prints the client's log on stderr.
Speed:   DM_PERF=1 prints how often and how long its drawing and network
         handling took, every minute and at exit (stderr).
         discord-messenger --bench runs a fixed workload without logging
         in and prints the time of each step, to compare machines or
         releases.  DM_VISUAL=default draws on the screen's default visual
         (8-bit dithered on most boards), DM_VISUAL=0x2b on the visual with
         that id (xdpyinfo lists them).  DM_NO_SHM=1 sends pixels over the
         X connection instead of shared memory; DM_NO_SCROLLCOPY=1 draws
         the whole message view when it scrolls instead of moving what is
         already on screen.

Source, and how it was built: https://github.com/atomchild411/dm
(branch irix; irix/dist has this package's recipe).

